# Convergence orders of composite trapezoid, Simpson and 4-node Gauss–Legendre quadrature

**Question.** Do the observed convergence orders of three composite rules match the theoretical 2, 4 and 8?
**Setup.** ∫₀¹ f for f = eˣ (exact e−1), 1/(1+25x²) (exact atan(5)/5) and √x (exact 2/3). Rules: composite trapezoid; composite Simpson (each of the *n* panels uses its two ends and midpoint); composite Gauss–Legendre with 4 nodes per panel (`numpy.polynomial.legendre.leggauss`). *n* = 2ᵏ panels, k = 1…12, float64, absolute error. For each function and rule, log(error) was regressed on log(*n*) by least squares over the points with error > 10⁻¹⁵ (exact zeros and rounding-level values such as 2.2·10⁻¹⁶ are excluded); order = −slope, 95 % interval = t(0.975, N−2) × standard error. Data: `results/errors.csv`, `results/fits.json`, `results/orders_table.md`, code `code/quad.py`, `code/quad_mp.py` and the interpretation `results/interpretation.md` in `experiment-repo` (results at commit `39a2856fe15d`, interpretation at `5e63fcfe9afc`). The last table column is a supplementary check with the same rules in 60-digit arithmetic (no roundoff floor).

